## 1. Mandatory Component Creation Workflow (`nextjs-component-dev`)

Whenever you are asked to create, scaffold, build, or implement **any new React or Next.js component** (including UI sections, cards, widgets, forms, or layout elements — whether requested directly by the user, required while building a page, or executed from `docs/plan/`):

1. **Always Activate & Read First**: You **MUST** read and follow [`.agents/skills/nextjs-component-dev/SKILL.md`](./.agents/skills/nextjs-component-dev/SKILL.md) before writing any component code. (If full UX/UI design discovery + adversarial QA orchestration is requested, use [`.agents/skills/nextjs-component-create/SKILL.md`](./.agents/skills/nextjs-component-create/SKILL.md), which delegates implementation to `nextjs-component-dev`).
2. **Non-Negotiable Standards from `nextjs-component-dev`**:
   - **Next.js Local Docs Lookup**: Query `node_modules\next\dist\docs` via `codebase-memory` MCP before authoring.
   - **Implementation Plan Gate**: Generate `implementation_plan.md` covering target path (`<new_component_dir>/<page_or_global>/<ComponentName>/`), TypeScript contracts with English TSDoc, translation keys, semantic tokens, and test cases.
   - **Dev Server Check**: Verify or start the Next.js dev server via `next-devtools` MCP (`nextjs_index`).
   - **Zero Hardcoded Strings (i18n)**: Populate `messages/[locale].json` across all `supported_languages` in `docs/project.json` first and consume via `next-intl` (`getTranslations` / `useTranslations`). Never hardcode copy or in-file fallback objects.
   - **TDD Baseline Delegation**: The `nextjs-test-author` agent authors `[ComponentName].test.tsx` (Jest + RTL + `jest-axe` + `NextIntlClientProvider`) before implementation. Implementation agents never write or edit tests.
   - **Component, Skeleton & Barrel**: Implement `[ComponentName].tsx` (RSC by default, push `"use client"` to leaf nodes), matching `[ComponentName]Skeleton.tsx` (mirroring geometry to prevent CLS), and `index.ts`.
   - **Semantic Tokens & Logical BiDi Styling**: Exclusively use semantic CSS variables from `app/globals.css` (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, `text-muted-foreground`) and Tailwind logical properties (`ms-`, `me-`, `ps-`, `pe-`, `start`, `end`). Physical directional classes (`ml-`, `mr-`, `pl-`, `pr-`, `left-`, `right-`) and raw hex/palette classes are strictly forbidden.
   - **Verification Gate**: Run `pwsh .agents/skills/nextjs-component-dev/scripts/verify-dev.ps1 -ComponentPath <target_component_dir>`, run targeted Playwright specs, and inspect runtime health via `next-devtools` MCP (`nextjs_call`).
   - **Plan Checklist Sync**: The orchestrator checks off completed component items (`- [x]`) in `docs/plan/05-pages-and-components.md`. Role agents never edit the plan.

